		<item>
		<title>BACK IN THE HI-808!</title>
		<link>http://bluescholars.com/blog/back-in-the-hi-808/</link>
		<comments>http://bluescholars.com/blog/back-in-the-hi-808/#comments</comments>
		<pubDate>Thu, 30 Jun 2011 05:19:21 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator>Geo</dc:creator>
				<category><![CDATA[Tourdates]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Bambu]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Blue Scholars]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Hawaii]]></category>

		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://bluescholars.com/blog/?p=3336</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[We're back in Hawai'i for a minute. Catch us at The Loft (Honolulu) w/ Bambu on Saturday, July 6 and hit the link for more events.]]></description>
			<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><a rel="attachment wp-att-3337" href="http://bluescholars.com/blog/back-in-the-hi-808/tumblr_lnevuh7jwc1qdestjo1_500/"><img class="size-full wp-image-3337 alignnone" title="tumblr_lnevuh7JWc1qdestjo1_500" src="http://bluescholars.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2011/06/tumblr_lnevuh7JWc1qdestjo1_500.jpg" alt="" width="415" height="641" /></a></p>
<p>We&#8217;re all back in Hawai&#8217;i for the first time since the <a href="http://02cd02a.netsolhost.com/blog/releases/oof-ep/">OOF! EP</a> release tour.</p>
<p>It gets active starting on Wednesday, July 6, kicking off with the <strong><a href="http://www.in4mants.com/hi/blog/prometheus-brown-bambu-walk-into-a-bar-album-release/">Prometheus Brown &amp; Bambu Walk Into A Bar in-store release party at In4mation Pearlridge</a></strong> from 4-5pm (all-ages, free!). From the 6th through the 8th, we&#8217;ll be posted up at the University of Hawaii-Manoa presenting workshops at the <strong><a href="http://essahawaii.tumblr.com/post/7171107630/rise-up-represent-july-6-8th-the-native">Rise Up! Represent! Student Conference</a></strong> (hit the link to register). To cap off the week, we&#8217;re rocking the <strong><a href="http://bluescholars.com/blog/tour-dates/">The Loft on Saturday night with Bambu, Omega Cix, DJ Packo and more</a></strong>.</p>
<p>Keep up with the crew on this trip via twitter: <a href="http://twitter.com/bluescholars">@bluescholars</a>, <a href="http://twitter.com/prometheusbrown">@prometheusbrown</a>, <a href="http://twitter.com/sabzi">@sabzi</a>, <a href="http://twitter.com/wongweezy">@wongweezy</a>, <a href="http://twitter.com/canhsolo">@canhsolo</a>.</p>
<p>In the meantime, <a href="http://www.youtube.com/prometheusbrown#g/c/2EE0FCE86107F7F2">check out video clips from the last Blue Scholars HI trip</a>.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
]]></content:encoded>
			<wfw:commentRss>http://bluescholars.com/blog/back-in-the-hi-808/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
		<slash:comments>1</slash:comments>
		</item>
		<item>
		<title>Untitled Kondabolu Brothers Project in Seattle (6/25 &amp; 6/26)</title>
		<link>http://bluescholars.com/blog/untitled-kondabolu-brothers-project-in-seattle-625-626/</link>
		<comments>http://bluescholars.com/blog/untitled-kondabolu-brothers-project-in-seattle-625-626/#comments</comments>
		<pubDate>Fri, 24 Jun 2011 03:36:36 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator>Geo</dc:creator>
				<category><![CDATA[Events]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[ashok kondabolu]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Blue Scholars]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Hari Kondabolu]]></category>

		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://bluescholars.com/blog/?p=3324</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[The Legendary Kondabolu Brothers of Queens, Hari (Comedy Central, Jimmy Kimmel Live) and Ashok ('Dap' from "Das Racist") bring their talk show, with little to no scripting, to Seattle's Theatre Off Jackson (409 7th Ave. S) on Saturday June 25th and Sunday June 26th.]]></description>
			<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><a href="http://www.brownpapertickets.com/event/180825"><img alt="" src="http://www.brownpapertickets.com/g/e/52980-250.gif" class="alignnone" width="220" height="332" /></a></p>
<p>Seattle: you mightv&#8217;e caught Hari at Sasquatch! or at his recent headlining runs at Comedy Underground or Kirkland Performance Center. You may have seen Ashok aka Dap onstage rapping at a <strong>Das Racist</strong> concert. But have you ever seen them together on the same stage at the same time? Doing a hilarious improv talk show? No, you haven&#8217;t! But this weekend, for the first time ever in Seattle, you can. </p>
<p>And we&#8217;ll be guest interviewees on Saturday&#8217;s show. Info and ticket links below:</p>
<p>&#8212;&#8212;&#8212;</p>
<blockquote><p>The Untitled Kondabolu Brothers Project in Seattle! (18+)<br />
Theatre Off Jackson<br />
Seattle, WA</p>
<p>The Legendary Kondabolu Brothers of Queens, Hari (Comedy Central, Jimmy Kimmel Live) and Ashok (&#8216;Dap&#8217; from &#8220;Das Racist&#8221;) bring their talk show, with little to no scripting, to Seattle&#8217;s Theatre Off Jackson (409 7th Ave. S) on Saturday June 25th and Sunday June 26th.</p>
<p>Tickets are $8 in advance and $12 at the door. (Ages 18 and over.)</p>
<p>Past topics have included: Peak Oil theory and the end of the world, the Illuminati, Blipsters, 7 foot tall Indo-Canadian basketball players, Germans and facial hair.</p>
<p>Some clips from previous shows: </p>
<p>Regarding Joel Stein of Time Magazine:<br />
<a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N9lxrpleEt8">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N9lxrpleEt8</a></p>
<p>Regarding &#8220;Blipsters&#8221;:<br />
<a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4Fbz1VXs4YM">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4Fbz1VXs4YM</a></p>
<p>Regarding Mustaches:<br />
<a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7BRTWy_T6S0">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7BRTWy_T6S0</a></p></blockquote>
]]></content:encoded>
			<wfw:commentRss>http://bluescholars.com/blog/untitled-kondabolu-brothers-project-in-seattle-625-626/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
		<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		</item>
