		<title>#CINE RELEASE SHOW SPECIAL GUEST: THE GOOD SIN</title>
		<link>http://bluescholars.com/blog/cine-release-party-special-guest-the-good-sin/</link>
		<comments>http://bluescholars.com/blog/cine-release-party-special-guest-the-good-sin/#comments</comments>
		<pubDate>Thu, 09 Jun 2011 20:03:28 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator>Hollis</dc:creator>
				<category><![CDATA[Uncategorized]]></category>

		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://bluescholars.com/blog/?p=3190</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[The Good Sin will perform along with Brothers From Another at the Cinemetropolis release party on Saturday, July 18. Check out his newest project Late, in collaboration with 10.4 Rog, and cop your ticket now!]]></description>
			<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><em>To help ring in Cinemetropolis at our release shows on June 17 and 18 at Neumos, we’ve hand-picked four of the best emerging Seattle acts and a couple of town-favorite hosts that we can’t wait to party with. We’ll be rolling out our supporting acts and hosts over this week to let you know who will be joining us to launch the new new.<br />
</em></p>
<p><a href="http://bluescholars.com/blog/cine-release-party-special-guest-the-good-sin/thegoodsin/" rel="attachment wp-att-3191"><img src="http://bluescholars.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2011/06/thegoodsin.jpeg" alt="" title="thegoodsin" width="500" height="333" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-3191" /></a></p>
<p><a href="http://thegoodsin.bandcamp.com"><img src="http://bluescholars.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2011/06/goodsinlate.jpeg" alt="" title="goodsinlate" width="350" height="350" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-3192" /></a></p>
<p>Joining us on Saturday, July 18, along with Brothers From Another is <strong>The Good Sin</strong>, whose collaboration with Renton&#8217;s 10.4 Rog resulted in <em>Late</em> (click above picture to stream and download). The Stranger&#8217;s Charles Mudede had <a href="http://www.thestranger.com/seattle/on-beats-and-sensitivity/Content?oid=6978239">this</a> to say about The Good Sin: </p>
<p><em><br />
<blockquote>The Good Sin is never loud or angry, but always at an emotional tempo that encourages thoughtfulness. There are angry thoughts, intellectual thoughts, and thoughtful thoughts—The Good Sin is defiantly about thoughtful thoughts concerning his world (working class), his relationships with women (which tend to be tender), and his spirituality (a kind of experimental theology). There is no meanness in The Good Sin&#8217;s rhymes, but neither is he simply positive about life. He recognizes the reality of social and historical problems, but he never lets these obstacles cloud or distort his humanism: &#8220;I&#8217;m counting on the sea view to tranquil the pain I&#8217;m having/Hoping love spreads through the year when the hate is happening/But I ain&#8217;t focused on the negative/It&#8217;s a blessing to know just how much to give&#8230;&#8221; (&#8220;All for You&#8221;).</p></blockquote>
<p></em></p>
<p>Make sure to get your <a href="https://www.etix.com/ticket/online/performanceSearch.jsp?performance_id=1476639&#038;cobrand=neumos">advanced tickets here</a> for Blue Scholars, Brothers From Another and The Good Sin on Saturday, July 18. </p>
<p>BLUE SCHOLARS<br />
CINEMETROPOLIS RELEASE PARTY<br />
JUNE 17 &#038; 18<br />
<a href="http://neumos.com">NEUMOS</a>, SEATTLE<br />
$15 ADVANCE<br />
ALL AGES</p>
]]></content:encoded>
